CRASH-18: restore the missing "else" in SMO_getSystemResult()

The period check sets error 422 (or 411 when the allocation fails), but the
block that seeks and freads the system values is not attached to the
if/else-if chain, so it runs on every error path with the result buffer
unallocated: fread writes through a NULL pointer when the period is -1 and
the function hands back a NULL buffer with a length of SysVars when the period
is past the end. Attach the block with "else", as in SMO_getLinkResult() and
the other result getters.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CRASH-18_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/output/swmm_output.c b/src/legacy/output/swmm_output.c
index 8a30764..b9287ba 100644
--- a/src/legacy/output/swmm_output.c
+++ b/src/legacy/output/swmm_output.c
@@ -1690,6 +1690,7 @@ int EXPORT_OPENSWMMCORE_OUTPUT_API SMO_getSystemResult(SMO_Handle p_handle, int
         errorcode = ERR422;
     else if MEMCHECK (temp = newFloatArray(p_data->SysVars))
         errorcode = ERR411;
